\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-2y)) \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y) \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-2y)) \\\\  & =-2{sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y)\\,i-2{sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323769 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323770 13194139534972 true] [17592186323769 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323771 13194139534972 true] [17592186323769 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323772 13194139534972 true] [17592186323769 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323773 13194139534972 true] [17592186323769 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323774 13194139534972 true] [17592186323769 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534972 true] [17592186323769 1041 "selection" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323769 1104 #edb/ref 17592186323774 13194139534972 true] [17592186323769 1110 #uuid "1fc36121-4553-5759-80a8-37f10821ef73" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323770 1034 "{sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y)\\,i-{sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y)\\,j" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323770 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534972 true] [17592186323770 1111 #uuid "17a82dea-a4d0-5418-8d80-ddd7fc43decd" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323771 1034 "x{sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y)\\,i-2y{sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y)\\,j" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323771 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534972 true] [17592186323771 1111 #uuid "65b17c73-f96d-58b3-ba74-036e204f51ca" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323772 1034 "\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x-2y)\\,i-2\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x-2y)\\,j" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323772 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534972 true] [17592186323772 1111 #uuid "f2724265-4796-5dcc-87a9-83ced534fcf7" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323773 1034 "-2\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x-2y)\\,i+\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x-2y)\\,j" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323773 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534972 true] [17592186323773 1111 #uuid "441bdf44-67a6-5746-b35e-310b1a1074ff" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323774 1034 "{sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y)\\,i-2{sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y)\\,j" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323774 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534972 true] [17592186323774 1111 #uuid "f4fbd5ae-a952-50f4-a41d-a4db7564ce14" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323775 1017 #edb/ref 17592186323776 13194139534972 true] [17592186323775 1089 "q-122619" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323775 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534972 true] [17592186323775 1100 "Which of the following diagrams represents the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)=x+{y}^{2}?$" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323775 1113 #uuid "40689dc7-e924-59ea-9bdd-9f2acdedd9ce" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323775 1145 "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =1 \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\,i+2y\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we have to sketch the vector field at the points $(-4,1),$ $(1,1),$ and $(3,-1).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the expression for $∇f.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(-4,1) & =i+2\\cdot 1\\,j=i+2\\,j \\\\ ∇f(1,1) & =i+2\\cdot 1\\,j=i+2\\,j \\\\ ∇f(3,-1) & =i+2\\cdot (-1)\\,j=i-2\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we draw the vectors starting at the corresponding points and obtain the following diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/1461b0737bf83fee8e16c1e5e102c36c2042e46935550ebc08a0d5774a561cd3.png)" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323776 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323777 13194139534972 true] [17592186323776 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323778 13194139534972 true] [17592186323776 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323779 13194139534