athacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/1461b0737bf83fee8e16c1e5e102c36c2042e46935550ebc08a0d5774a561cd3.png" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323781 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534972 true] [17592186323781 1111 #uuid "bc0d1654-e23b-5e72-a437-76d5fc83daae" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323782 1017 #edb/ref 17592186323783 13194139534972 true] [17592186323782 1089 "q-122699" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323782 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534972 true] [17592186323782 1100 "Which of the following diagrams represents the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)=2y-x?$" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323782 1113 #uuid "bef9da0c-f04d-5f81-acd5-4bdc3f69bc23" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323782 1145 "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2y-x) \\\\  & =-1 \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2y-x) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =-i+2\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we have to sketch the vector field at the points $(-2,2),$ $(2,2),$ and $(2,-2).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the expression for $∇f.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(-2,2) & =-i+2\\,j \\\\ ∇f(2,2) & =-i+2\\,j \\\\ ∇f(2,-2) & =-i+2\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we draw the vectors starting at the corresponding points and obtain the following diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/92f46798ebeae9017c91ddae24e0f68cef81a1045314950bc4b56af003af0b42.png)" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323783 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323784 13194139534972 true] [17592186323783 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323785 13194139534972 true] [17592186323783 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323786 13194139534972 true] [17592186323783 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323787 13194139534972 true] [17592186323783 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323788 13194139534972 true] [17592186323783 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534972 true] [17592186323783 1041 "selection" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323783 1104 #edb/ref 17592186323786 13194139534972 true] [17592186323783 1110 #uuid "cd745c4b-76db-5536-a918-e965edb45b2b" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323784 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/df6472974d246217341c69163c2336190980b5aacaa5b1a5c11cbb7126ddde86.png" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323784 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534972 true] [17592186323784 1111 #uuid "3648a022-3fb7-5a0b-a02e-2822033cfc59" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323785 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/6c76d43daa86b2c8034e3f12592ee6c18bc533034cb255934ff7eb08b2d53623.png" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323785 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534972 true] [17592186323785 1111 #uuid "d24f51e8-9ff8-51ce-9a27-8dcb023c627c" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323786 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/92f46798ebeae9017c91ddae24e0f68cef81a1045314950bc4b56af003af0b42.png" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323786 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534972 true] [17592186323786 1111 #uuid "6147ad45-5d20-5769-ac9e-6d01c7d98d74" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323787 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/7618ae208ba53f12fb31988a3e0d0cb40f78ddc4348c5049bb09127039c4d965.png" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323787 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534972 true] [17592186323787 1111 #uuid "32448c40-e06a-58e3-be5a-38374fc25c69" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323788 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/0f45b194df67a060c195d4368050cdad9b8bfefab86b41d5eb63723631543d7b.png" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323788 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534972 true] [17592186323788 1111 #uuid "87777c72-a74c-596f-b251-14e9d73f7a3f" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323789 1017 #edb/ref 17592186323790 13194139534972 true] [17592186323789 1089 "q-122713" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323789 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534972 true] [17592186323789 1100 "Which of the following diagrams represents the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)=2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(xy)?$" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323789 1113 #uuid "91cb20d9-0768-57d2-91f5-f873cc45139d" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323789 1145 "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(xy)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2y}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+1} \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(xy)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{2y}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+1}\\,i+\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+1}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we have to sketch the vector field at the points $(-1,1),$ $(0,-2),$ and $(2,0).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the expression for $∇f.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(-1,1) & =\\frac{2\\cdot 1}{(-1)^{2}(1)^{2}+1}\\,i+\\frac{2\\cdot (-1)}{(-1)^{2}(1)^{2}+1}\\,j=i-j \\\\ ∇f(0,-2) & =\\frac{2\\cdot (-2)}{(0)^{2}(-2)^{2}+1}\\,i+\\frac{2\\cdot 0}{(0)^{2}(-2)^{2}+1}\\,j=-4\\,i \\\\ ∇f(2,0) & =\\frac{2\\cdot 0}{(2)^{2}(0)^{2}+1}\\,i+\\frac{2\\cdot 2}{(2)^{2}(0)^{2}+1}\\,j=4\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we draw the vectors starting at the corresponding points and obtain the following diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/1da33de6ab53eee30cb7dbdba61a437fd9e3209437d061d2c546386981962942.png)" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323790 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323791 13194139534972 true] [17592186323790 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323792 13194139534972 true] [17592186323790 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323793 13194139534972 true] [17592186323790 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323794 13194139534972 true] [17592186323790 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323795 13194139534972 true] [17592186323790 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534972 true] [17592186323790 1041 "selection" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323790 1104 #edb/ref 17592186323793 13194139534972 true] [17592186323790 1110 #uuid "02af614d-c2ab-5b63-b7e7-f5ec5151a789" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323791 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/5e19f0874cbbfcf99c45951c98b19d941c39451c33887fbdcacdb75faeffdc57.png" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323791 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534972 true] [17592186323791 1111 #uuid "c902c70b-91c1-5148-8e26-b124c1fbcc9d" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323792 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/8270942dbaed9f5177e179104bb479802a39c48afa2a528b138b458c042a1556.png" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323792 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534972 true] [17592186323792 1111 #uuid "2b775338-e720-5c2e-90ff-59e0453c2ed9" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323793 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/1da33de6ab53eee30cb7dbdba61a437fd9e3209437d061d2c546386981962942.png" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323793 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534972 true] [17592186323793 1111 #uuid "1d2f433f-6671-52e7-944a-ec2f91e6444f" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323794 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-captur