3815 1111 #uuid "337d4011-cdb5-5fc4-86ce-59025a5b0cf0" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323816 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/9ce2dd3e0c639e4f520556c7f4955451eb599b35e0714aa326cb6efd74cfaa5c.png" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323816 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534972 true] [17592186323816 1111 #uuid "7eaa7c09-0cdb-5a78-9538-d0429a53d266" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323817 1017 #edb/ref 17592186323818 13194139534972 true] [17592186323817 1089 "q-122834" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323817 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534972 true] [17592186323817 1100 "Which of the following could be the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)={x}^{2}-{y}^{2}?$" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323817 1113 #uuid "ec7c19a9-6da7-55d6-b075-dc647a76929b" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323817 1145 "We start by plotting some level curves of the function:\n\n- Setting $f(x,y)=-1,$ we get ${x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=-1,$ which gives the vertical hyperbola ${y}^{2}-{x}^{2}=1$\n\n- Setting $f(x,y)=0,$ we get ${x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=0,$ which gives the pair of lines $y=\\pm x$\n\n- Setting $f(x,y)=2,$ we get ${x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=2,$ which gives the horizontal hyperbola $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=1$\n\n- $⋯$\n\nContinuing in this way, we get the following contour plot:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/cecc7f28c20523aac9f153022d64da4233ce995e05df3b3e2886b7fb3b20d089.png)\n\nNote that $f(x,y)$ increases as we move from left to right in the right half-plane $x>0,$ and increases as we move from right-to-left in the left half-plane $x<0.$\n\nNow, we recall the following facts:\n\n- The gradient field vectors of a function $f(x,y)$ always lie perpendicular to its level curves.\n\n- Moreover, the vectors point in the direction where $f(x,y)$ increases.\n\nWith this in mind, we can add the vector field to the contour plot, giving the following picture.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/037f46d3fdd190749c2aefe51222475fdd337a7b3ce53e6809048e3491a31a47.png)\n\nSo, the corresponding gradient field is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/346e6bb41b8dd3b353dfedbc55eb25690396d5492d18199ba99a12523452db0a.png)" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323818 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323819 13194139534972 true] [17592186323818 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323820 13194139534972 true] [17592186323818 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323821 13194139534972 true] [17592186323818 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323822 13194139534972 true] [17592186323818 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323823 13194139534972 true] [17592186323818 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534972 true] [17592186323818 1041 "selection" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323818 1104 #edb/ref 17592186323820 13194139534972 true] [17592186323818 1110 #uuid "a0456780-40a1-514d-9f84-3c653e868a7d" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323819 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/e76b318c2f347bc59746ea0dc88c838ad46694724563867a0ee94318c826d887.png" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323819 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534972 true] [17592186323819 1111 #uuid "23fc4ad8-5a2a-57f4-b15e-7970bebec82d" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323820 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/346e6bb41b8dd3b353dfedbc55eb25690396d5492d18199ba99a12523452db0a.png" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323820 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534972 true] [17592186323820 1111 #uuid "7a00d1e7-85b4-568b-964d-d7f749fac776" 13194139534972 true] [17592186323821 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/57f5858f1ccae96a1